# UVDAR LED model for the MRS x500, four-sided, PX4 motor aligned, WITH beacon.
# x500 counterpart of uvdar_core's config/models/quadrotor_beacon.txt.
#
# The first eight rows are identical to x500_foursided_px4_motor_aligned.txt --
# see that file for the arm layout and the per-arm signal mapping.
#
# BEACON: four LEDs on top of the vehicle, 0.125 m above the arm plane, 10 mm
# from the centre and aimed +X, +Y, -X, -Y, all carrying signal_id 4. They sit
# well within uvdar_core's 3 cm LED grouping distance, so BodyModel merges them
# into one marker at (0, 0, 0.125) that is visible from any azimuth.
#
# Derived from `--enable-uv-leds-beacon signal_id:=4` in mrs_uav_gazebo_simulator's
# x500.sdf.jinja / uv_devices.sdf.jinja (same geometry as ROS1's x500 beacon).
# The beacon's signal_id must stay distinct from the four arm IDs: BodyModel
# refuses a signal that appears on more than one LED group. It needs a 5th
# line in uvdar_gazebo_plugin/config/sequences/default.txt and a 5th entry in
# tracking.sequences.
#
# Type is 1 for the beacon rows to follow ROS1's quadrotor_beacon.txt; the ROS2
# BodyModel stores the column but does not use it. Pitch is 0.0 for the same
# reason given in x500_foursided_px4_motor_aligned.txt.
#
# X Y Z Type Pitch Yaw signal_id
